'''tetrabranchiate''' (tet-ra-brang′ki-āt), ''a.'' and ''n.'' [< NL. ''tetrabranchiatus'', < Gr. τετρα-, four, + βράγχια, gills.] Same as ''tetrabranch.''

'''tetracamarous''' (tet-ra-kam′a-rus), ''a.'' [< Gr. τετρα-, four, + καμάρα, a vault.] In ''bot.'', having four closed carpels.

'''tetracarpellary''' (tet-ra-kär′pe-lā-ri), ''a.'' [< Gr. τετρα-, four, + NL. ''carpellum'', carpel, + ''-ary.''] In ''bot.'', having four carpels.

'''Tetracaulodon''' (tet-rạ-kâ′lọ̄-don), ''n.'' [NL. (Godman), < Gr. τετρα-, four, + καυλός, stem, + ὀδούς, tooth.] A genus of mastodons. See ''Mastodontinæ.''

